@spec menu_spec  src=tests/specs/menu_spec.lua  loc=354  cases=14
@exercises commandManager (mgr), menu (menu)
@surface   mgr:installManifest, mgr:installTree, mgr:register, mgr:scope, mgr:push, menu:isOpen, mgr:invoke, mgr:keysFor, menu:level, mgr:entry, menu:press, menu:close, mgr:surface, menu:path, mgr:beginPrefix, mgr:appendPrefix, mgr:isPrefixActive, mgr:letterCapture

# Intent
  The lotus menu as a scope. Opening pushes a modal cmgr scope, so a letter typed during
  the walk cannot reach a page verb, and closing pops it. What survives the walk is
  declared by group: the transport, because Continuum is played while it is edited, and
  the page switchers, because travel is not a menu letter. The set is built from the
  stack at the moment the menu opens, so the tracker's own transport verbs pass through
  while the tracker is showing. The close verb is registered on the menu's own scope, so
  the gate is its own guard — Esc reaches it only while the menu is up, and the open verb
  is blocked by the scope it pushed. See design/lotus-menu.md § What stays live.

# Helpers
  @fn fixture(page)  @ 18-34
      -- A cmgr carrying the real manifest, stub bodies for the verbs the cases invoke, and the
      -- menu built over it, with the tracker page on the stack. Each body logs its name, so a
      -- gated-out invoke reads as silence rather than as a return value.
  @fn node(name, children)  @ 37-39
      -- One tree node in the shape manifest.lua's `item` builds.
  @fn synthetic()  @ 44-54
      -- A synthetic surface for the rules a level obeys whatever is declared: one global verb two
      -- levels down, one page verb at the top. The real manifest carries no witness for these, so
      -- re-cutting a path there moves nothing here.
  @fn titles(members)  @ 56-60
  @fn named(members, title)  @ 62-64

# Cases
  @case 'opening pushes the menu scope over the page, and closing pops it'  [pure]  @ 68-81
  @case 'a page verb is blocked while the menu is open, and live again after'  [pure]  @ 87-101
  @case 'the transport and the page switchers stay live through the walk'  [pure]  @ 107-118
  @case 'each verb is guarded by the scope it is registered on'  [pure]  @ 122-131
  @case 'the top level holds the reachable groups and the leaves of one-segment paths'  [pure]  @ 138-157
  @case 'a group is a member where it or a descendant holds a reachable entry'  [pure]  @ 165-180
  @case 'a level omits what the stack cannot reach'  [pure]  @ 186-199
  @case 'a level lists its groups in tree order, then its leaves by title'  [pure]  @ 206-228
  @case 'the level is read from the surface the menu snapshotted as it opened'  [pure]  @ 234-249
  @case 'a letter descends into a group, and invokes a leaf'  [pure]  @ 257-270
  @case 'Esc pops one level, and closes the menu from the top'  [pure]  @ 276-294
  @case 'a pending prefix survives the walk, and the leaf takes it'  [pure]  @ 301-315
  @case 'the scope declares a dismissal that closes the walk outright'  [pure]  @ 321-331
  @case 'the open menu is what captures a letter'  [pure]  @ 338-352

